decision: changes-requested

## Review summary

Two medium blockers remain: the shim can block while publishing a large PID report, and a cleanup inspection error can leave descendants alive after dispatcher death. The manuals and recorded containment limits also describe the shimless environment scan as the normal Linux path; I recorded that as a low follow-up.

The focused Go tests and `go vet` passed. `surface-check` passed with zero findings, and `artifact-check` exited 0. Both strict validation commands ran but could not build because the read-only sandbox blocked Go temporary-workdir and cache writes; I relied on the sealed passing build, e2e, integration, and unit evidence. `review-check` and `closeout-check` are deferred because they require an attestation, which this review is not authorized to record.

The review rules applied were security, backend-go, and documentation-style. No repository changes were made; the worktree remains clean.

